<h1>About Valora</h1>
<p style="font-size:18px;max-width:720px;">Valora is a trade marketplace built on a simple idea: the things you no longer need are exactly what someone else is looking for. Instead of haggling over prices, trade them.</p>

<div class="about-grid">
  <div class="about-card">
    <h3>🔄 Trade, don't just buy</h3>
    <p>List an item and receive offers of other items in exchange. Every offer can include <strong>cash on top</strong> to balance out the difference in value.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="about-card">
    <h3>🏷️ New &amp; used</h3>
    <p>Every listing is clearly marked as new or used across six categories: Cars, Tools, Jewelry, Clothes, Home Goods, and Other.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="about-card">
    <h3>🤝 You stay in control</h3>
    <p>Review every offer on your listings, accept the one you like best, decline the rest. Withdrawing an offer you made is always free.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="fee-box">
  <h2>How the 5% fee works</h2>
  <p>Valora is free to join and free to list. We earn money only when a trade actually happens: we collect a <strong>5% platform fee on the cash portion</strong> of each completed trade.</p>
  <p>Example: you trade your guitar for someone's keyboard plus <strong>$200 cash on top</strong> — the fee is <strong>$10</strong>. If a trade involves <strong>no cash at all</strong>, there is <strong>no fee</strong>.</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0;">The fee is paid securely by card at the moment the trade completes.</p>
</div>

<h2>Our story</h2>
<p style="max-width:720px;">Valora was founded by <strong>Zrek</strong>, who believed trading should be as easy as buying. No endless negotiations, no wasted listings — just a fair swap between people, with a little cash on top when it makes sense.</p>

